<title>THAILAND: Stable baht before fixing change - finance minister.</title>
<headline>Stable baht before fixing change - finance minister.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1996-12-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finance Minister Amnuay Viravan said on Thursday Thailand's daily fixing of the baht should be made flexible in the future but stressed any change must not be at the expense of the currency's stability.</p>
<p>Amnuay told bankers and businessmen that Thailand should stop relying on domestic interest rates as the sole mechanism for managing the baht, foreign capital flows and money supply.</p>
</text>
